.Sh CAVEATS
Most functions mark a
.Dv nullptr
.Fa buf Ns .mem ,
or a
.Dv nullptr
.Fa allocator Ns .allocator ,
as unreachable rather than checking it.
In particular, calling
.Fn xft_vec_destroy ,
.Fn xft_vec_push_back ,
.Fn xft_vec_extend ,
.Fn xft_vec_popmv
or
.Fn xft_vec_remove
on a vector whose creation failed is undefined behavior.
.Pp
.Fn xft_vec_push_back
assumes the capacity is at least
.Fa type_size ,
which holds for vectors made by
.Fn xft_new_vec
with the same
.Fa type_size .
.Fa data
must not point into the vector itself, since growth may free it.
.Pp
Index arithmetic in the accessors is not checked for overflow.
.Pp
.Fn xft_vec_pop_managed
is declared
.Ql always_inline
in
.In vec.h
without being
.Ql inline ,
so GCC warns
.Pq Fl Wattributes
at call sites in other translation units.
